   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_usart.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *          functionalities of the Universal synchronous asynchronous receiver
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *          transmitter (USART):           
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Initialization and Configuration
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Data transfers
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Multi-Processor Communication
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + LIN mode
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Half-duplex mode
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Smartcard mode
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + IrDA mode
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + DMA transfers management
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management 
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   *           
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   @verbatim       
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable peripheral clock using the following functions
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           RCC_APB2PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB2Periph_USARTx, ENABLE) for USART1 and USART6 
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_USARTx, ENABLE) for USART2, USART3, 
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           UART4 or UART5.
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccdQ2tkR.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) According to the USART mode, enable the GPIO clocks using 
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           RCC_AHB1PeriphClockCmd() function. (The I/O can be TX, RX, CTS, 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           or/and SCLK). 
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Peripheral's alternate function: 
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Connect the pin to the desired peripherals' Alternate 
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****             Function (AF) using GPIO_PinAFConfig() function
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Configure the desired pin in alternate function by:
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****             GPIO_InitStruct->GPIO_Mode = GPIO_Mode_AF
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Select the type, pull-up/pull-down and output speed via 
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****             GPIO_PuPd, GPIO_OType and GPIO_Speed members
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Call GPIO_Init() function
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the Baud Rate, Word Length , Stop Bit, Parity, Hardware 
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           flow control and Mode(Receiver/Transmitter) using the USART_Init()
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           function.
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) For synchronous mode, enable the clock and program the polarity,
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           phase and last bit using the USART_ClockInit() function.
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the NVIC and the corresponding interrupt using the function 
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****          USART_ITConfig() if you need to use interrupt mode. 
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) When using the DMA mode 
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Configure the DMA using DMA_Init() function
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Active the needed channel Request using USART_DMACmd() function
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the USART using the USART_Cmd() function.
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the DMA using the DMA_Cmd() function, when using DMA mode. 
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       -@- Refer to Multi-Processor, LIN, half-duplex, Smartcard, IrDA sub-sections
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           for more details
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]        
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     In order to reach higher communication baudrates, it is possible to
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     enable the oversampling by 8 mode using the function USART_OverSampling8Cmd().
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This function should be called after enabling the USART clock (RCC_APBxPeriphClockCmd())
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     and before calling the function USART_Init().
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****             
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     @endverbatim        
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   ******************************************************************************
