 131:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** /** @defgroup USART_Group1 Initialization and Configuration functions
 132:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *  @brief   Initialization and Configuration functions 
 133:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *
 134:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @verbatim   
 135:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
 136:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****             ##### Initialization and Configuration functions #####
 137:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 138:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 139:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to initialize the USART 
 140:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     in asynchronous and in synchronous modes.
 141:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (+) For the asynchronous mode only these parameters can be configured: 
 142:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Baud Rate
 143:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Word Length 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccdQ2tkR.s 			page 4


 144:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Stop Bit
 145:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Parity: If the parity is enabled, then the MSB bit of the data written
 146:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****              in the data register is transmitted but is changed by the parity bit.
 147:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****              Depending on the frame length defined by the M bit (8-bits or 9-bits),
 148:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****              the possible USART frame formats are as listed in the following table:
 149:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    +-------------------------------------------------------------+     
 150:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |   M bit |  PCE bit  |            USART frame                |
 151:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |---------------------|---------------------------------------|             
 152:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |    0    |    0      |    | SB | 8 bit data | STB |          |
 153:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|  
 154:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |    0    |    1      |    | SB | 7 bit data | PB | STB |     |
 155:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|  
 156:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |    1    |    0      |    | SB | 9 bit data | STB |          |
 157:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|  
 158:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    |    1    |    1      |    | SB | 8 bit data | PB | STB |     |
 159:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****    +-------------------------------------------------------------+            
 160:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Hardware flow control
 161:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Receiver/transmitter modes
 162:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 163:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 164:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     The USART_Init() function follows the USART  asynchronous configuration 
 165:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     procedure (details for the procedure are available in reference manual (RM0090)).
 166:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 167:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****      (+) For the synchronous mode in addition to the asynchronous mode parameters these 
 168:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****          parameters should be also configured:
 169:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART Clock Enabled
 170:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART polarity
 171:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART phase
 172:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART LastBit
 173:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   
 174:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 175:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     These parameters can be configured using the USART_ClockInit() function.
 176:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 177:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @endverbatim
 178:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @{
 179:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   */
