 522:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** /** @defgroup USART_Group2 Data transfers functions
 523:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *  @brief   Data transfers functions 
 524:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *
 525:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @verbatim   
 526:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
 527:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****                       ##### Data transfers functions #####
 528:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 529:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 530:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the USART data 
 531:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     transfers.
 532:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 533:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     During an USART reception, data shifts in least significant bit first through 
 534:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     the RX pin. In this mode, the USART_DR register consists of a buffer (RDR) 
 535:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     between the internal bus and the received shift register.
 536:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 537:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     When a transmission is taking place, a write instruction to the USART_DR register 
 538:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     stores the data in the TDR register and which is copied in the shift register 
 539:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     at the end of the current transmission.
 540:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 541:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     The read access of the USART_DR register can be done using the USART_ReceiveData()
 542:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     function and returns the RDR buffered value. Whereas a write access to the USART_DR 
 543:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     can be done using USART_SendData() function and stores the written data into 
 544:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     TDR buffer.
 545:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 546:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @endverbatim
 547:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @{
 548:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   */
 549:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
