 586:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** /** @defgroup USART_Group3 MultiProcessor Communication functions
 587:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *  @brief   Multi-Processor Communication functions 
 588:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *
 589:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @verbatim   
 590:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
 591:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****               ##### Multi-Processor Communication functions #####
 592:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 593:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 594:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the USART 
 595:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     multiprocessor communication.
 596:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 597:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     For instance one of the USARTs can be the master, its TX output is connected 
 598:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     to the RX input of the other USART. The others are slaves, their respective 
 599:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     TX outputs are logically ANDed together and connected to the RX input of the 
 600:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     master.
 601:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 602:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     USART multiprocessor communication is possible through the following procedure:
 603:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the Baud rate, Word length = 9 bits, Stop bits, Parity, Mode 
 604:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           transmitter or Mode receiver and hardware flow control values using 
 605:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           the USART_Init() function.
 606:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Configures the USART address using the USART_SetAddress() function.
 607:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Configures the wake up method (USART_WakeUp_IdleLine or USART_WakeUp_AddressMark)
 608:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           using USART_WakeUpConfig() function only for the slaves.
 609:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the USART using the USART_Cmd() function.
 610:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enter the USART slaves in mute mode using USART_ReceiverWakeUpCmd() function.
 611:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 612:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     The USART Slave exit from mute mode when receive the wake up condition.
 613:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 614:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @endverbatim
 615:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @{
 616:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   */
 617:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
