 691:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****                         ##### LIN mode functions #####
 692:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 693:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 694:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the USART LIN 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccdQ2tkR.s 			page 30


 695:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     Mode communication.
 696:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 697:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     In LIN mode, 8-bit data format with 1 stop bit is required in accordance with 
 698:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     the LIN standard.
 699:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 700:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     Only this LIN Feature is supported by the USART IP:
 701:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (+) LIN Master Synchronous Break send capability and LIN slave break detection
 702:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           capability :  13-bit break generation and 10/11 bit break detection
 703:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 704:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 705:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     USART LIN Master transmitter communication is possible through the following 
 706:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     procedure:
 707:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the Baud rate, Word length = 8bits, Stop bits = 1bit, Parity, 
 708:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         Mode transmitter or Mode receiver and hardware flow control values using 
 709:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         the USART_Init() function.
 710:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the USART using the USART_Cmd() function.
 711:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the LIN mode using the USART_LINCmd() function.
 712:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Send the break character using USART_SendBreak() function.
 713:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 714:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     USART LIN Master receiver communication is possible through the following procedure:
 715:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the Baud rate, Word length = 8bits, Stop bits = 1bit, Parity, 
 716:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           Mode transmitter or Mode receiver and hardware flow control values using 
 717:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           the USART_Init() function.
 718:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the USART using the USART_Cmd() function.
 719:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Configures the break detection length using the USART_LINBreakDetectLengthConfig()
 720:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           function.
 721:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Enable the LIN mode using the USART_LINCmd() function.
 722:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 723:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       -@- In LIN mode, the following bits must be kept cleared:
 724:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****        (+@) CLKEN in the USART_CR2 register,
 725:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****        (+@) STOP[1:0], SCEN, HDSEL and IREN in the USART_CR3 register.
 726:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 727:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @endverbatim
 728:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @{
 729:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   */
