 859:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** /** @defgroup USART_Group6 Smartcard mode functions
 860:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *  @brief   Smartcard mode functions 
 861:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  *
 862:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @verbatim   
 863:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================
 864:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****                               ##### Smartcard mode functions #####
 865:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****  ===============================================================================  
 866:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 867:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     This subsection provides a set of functions allowing to manage the USART 
 868:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     Smartcard communication.
 869:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 870:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     The Smartcard interface is designed to support asynchronous protocol Smartcards as
 871:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     defined in the ISO 7816-3 standard.
 872:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 873:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     The USART can provide a clock to the smartcard through the SCLK output.
 874:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     In smartcard mode, SCLK is not associated to the communication but is simply derived 
 875:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     from the internal peripheral input clock through a 5-bit prescaler.
 876:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     [..]
 877:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     Smartcard communication is possible through the following procedure:
 878:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Configures the Smartcard Prescaler using the USART_SetPrescaler() function.
 879:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Configures the Smartcard Guard Time using the USART_SetGuardTime() function.
 880:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the USART clock using the USART_ClockInit() function as following:
 881:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART Clock enabled
 882:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART CPOL Low
 883:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART CPHA on first edge
 884:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) USART Last Bit Clock Enabled
 885:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) Program the Smartcard interface using the USART_Init() function as following:
 886:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Word Length = 9 Bits
 887:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) 1.5 Stop Bit
 888:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Even parity
 889:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) BaudRate = 12096 baud
 890:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Hardware flow control disabled (RTS and CTS signals)
 891:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (++) Tx and Rx enabled
 892:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) POptionally you can enable the parity error interrupt using the USART_ITConfig()
 893:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           function
 894:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) PEnable the USART using the USART_Cmd() function.
 895:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) PEnable the Smartcard NACK using the USART_SmartCardNACKCmd() function.
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccdQ2tkR.s 			page 36


 896:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       (#) PEnable the Smartcard interface using the USART_SmartCardCmd() function.
 897:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 898:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****     Please refer to the ISO 7816-3 specification for more details.
 899:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 900:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       -@- It is also possible to choose 0.5 stop bit for receiving but it is recommended 
 901:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           to use 1.5 stop bits for both transmitting and receiving to avoid switching 
 902:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           between the two configurations.
 903:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       -@- In smartcard mode, the following bits must be kept cleared:
 904:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (+@) LINEN bit in the USART_CR2 register.
 905:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****         (+@) HDSEL and IREN bits in the USART_CR3 register.
 906:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****       -@- Smartcard mode is available on USART peripherals only (not available on UART4 
 907:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****           and UART5 peripherals).
 908:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** 
 909:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c **** @endverbatim
 910:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   * @{
 911:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_usart.c ****   */
